{
    "background_story": "Shepherd was a young monk living in a secluded monastery, dedicated to a life of spiritual contemplation. For years, he followed the strict routines and rituals, seeking enlightenment. However, he began to feel a growing sense of disconnection from the world beyond the monastery's walls. One day, while on a solo retreat in the mountains, Shepherd stumbled upon a hidden village ravaged by poverty and suffering. Witnessing the struggles of the villagers firsthand, he felt a profound awakening. He realized that true spirituality wasn't just about personal enlightenment, but about serving others and making a positive impact on the world. Shepherd left the monastery to dedicate his life to helping those in need, using his skills to build sustainable communities and bring hope to those who had lost it. His awakening marked the beginning of a new journey, one that would bring him closer to the world and to his true purpose.",
